---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../../components/HeroSection.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="FAQ" lang="en">

  <HeroSection
    headline="Every Question, Answered"
    subtitle="The objections are predictable. The answers are backed by data, law, and historical precedent."
  />

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="space-y-12">

      <!-- Q1 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"Iran is too far away"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            Hawaii is 2,400 miles from the mainland. Alaska is separated by all of Canada. Guam is 6,000 miles away. Iran is 7,243 miles from Washington, D.C. — in the age of modern aviation and telecommunications, this is logistics, not a barrier.
          </p>
          <p>
            The US already maintains <span class="font-bold text-navy">750 military installations across 80 countries</span>. Non-contiguity has never been a constitutional requirement for statehood.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q2 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"It would be too expensive"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            Iran sits on <span class="font-bold text-navy">$27.3 trillion in natural resources</span> — the 3rd largest oil reserves and 2nd largest natural gas reserves on Earth. When sanctions were eased in 2016, Iran's GDP grew 12.5% in a single year.
          </p>
          <p>
            Post-WWII Germany and Japan were devastated nations with no oil. They became the 3rd and 4th largest economies on Earth under American investment. <span class="font-bold text-navy">Iran is starting with more resources than either of them had.</span>
          </p>
          <p>
            The US currently spends $20-50 billion per year on Gulf military bases to contain Iran. As a state, that spending drops to zero.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q3 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"They don't share our values"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            Cyrus the Great issued the first declaration of human rights in 539 BCE. Thomas Jefferson owned and recommended his biography. Iran's Constitutional Revolution of 1906 was the first in the Islamic world. Women gained suffrage in 1963.
          </p>
          <p>
            According to the GAMAAN survey, <span class="font-bold text-navy">89% of Iranians support democracy</span>. Only 40% identify as Muslim — vs. the regime's claim of 99.5%. 73% advocate separation of religion and state. Iran's fertility rate (1.7) is below replacement level — characteristic of secular, modernized societies.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Iranian people have been fighting for democratic values continuously: 2009, 2017, 2019, 2022, 2025, 2026. <span class="font-bold text-navy">The regime is the obstacle, not the people.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q4 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"It's never been done before"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            It has been done — repeatedly. Vermont was an independent republic for 14 years before joining in 1791. Texas was an independent republic for 10 years before joining in 1845. Hawaii was an independent kingdom for nearly a century before becoming a state in 1959.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Louisiana Purchase incorporated French and Spanish-speaking populations. The Mexican Cession incorporated Spanish-speaking populations. Alaska was bought from Russia. <span class="font-bold text-navy">37 territories have joined the Union. The playbook exists.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q5 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"What about the language barrier?"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            The United States has no official language at the federal level. Louisiana was predominantly French-speaking when it became a state in 1812. New Mexico was Spanish-speaking in 1912 — laws are still published in both languages today.
          </p>
          <p>
            Farsi is an <span class="font-bold text-navy">Indo-European language</span> — linguistically closer to English than Arabic, Turkish, or any East Asian language. Iran ranks #68 globally on the EF English Proficiency Index, slightly above the global average. English is already taught in Iranian secondary schools.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q6 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"What about nuclear weapons?"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            Statehood is the <span class="font-bold text-navy">only permanent solution</span> to Iran's nuclear program. As a US state, all nuclear materials fall under federal authority (DOE, NRC). Enrichment capabilities convert to civilian nuclear energy under full regulation.
          </p>
          <p>
            No treaty to renegotiate. No sunset clauses. No withdrawal provisions. Both sides proved with the JCPOA that treaties can be abrogated. <span class="font-bold text-navy">Statehood is constitutionally permanent.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q7 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"90 million people would have too many representatives"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            The 435-seat cap in the House is a law, not a constitutional requirement. Congress could expand it — and many political scientists already argue it should be.
          </p>
          <p>
            Iran could also be admitted as <span class="font-bold text-navy">4-6 separate states</span> based on its diverse ethnic and geographic regions — Azerbaijan, Kurdistan, Fars, Khorasan, Baluchistan — each comparable in population to existing large states.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Louisiana Purchase roughly doubled the entire land area of the United States. America has absorbed massive additions before.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q8 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"What about security concerns?"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            The US turned its three most dangerous enemies into its closest allies. Germany, Japan, and South Korea now host 119, 120, and 73 US installations respectively — and became the world's 3rd, 4th, and 10th largest economies.
          </p>
          <p>
            Iran borders Iraq, Afghanistan, Pakistan, Turkey, and five other nations. It controls the northern shore of the Strait of Hormuz, through which 20% of the world's oil flows. <span class="font-bold text-navy">This is not a liability — it is the most strategic real estate on the planet.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Q9 -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-black text-navy mb-4">"Iranian-Americans already prove this works"</h3>
        <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>
            The 1-2 million Iranian-Americans in the US are living proof of cultural compatibility. <span class="font-bold text-navy">65% hold a bachelor's degree or higher</span> (vs. 33% US average). 27% hold a master's or PhD — the highest of any ethnic group in America.
          </p>
          <p>
            Median household income: <span class="font-bold text-navy">$97,046</span> — 39% above the US median. 33,570 active business owners generating $2.56 billion. Only 20% of second-generation marry fellow Iranians — deep, organic assimilation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-navy py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <p class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-8">Ready to see how it actually works?</p>
      <a
        href="/en/the-process/"
        class="inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-black text-lg px-10 py-5 rounded-xl hover:bg-gold-light transition-colors shadow-lg shadow-gold/20"
      >
        The constitutional process
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
